          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022log.md\u0022}"
        }
      ],
      "assistant_text": "Now I can see the relationship clearly. These two pages describe complementary aspects of how Grimoire isolates and centralizes key architectural concerns:\n\n**Credential-scoping** isolates **who** holds sensitive data \u2014 credentials are scoped to the specific child process that needs them, never held by the Hub itself.\n\n**Runtime-paths** isolates **where** all file locations are determined \u2014 they\u0027re resolved once at startup from a single point, never scattered or rediscovered throughout the codebase.\n\nTogether, they represent a pattern: **centralized configuration and resolution of runtime concerns, paired with strict scoping of access to those resolved values**. Both decisions prevent leakage (whether of credentials or path logic) by ensuring that sensitive decisions are made once, in one place, and then scoped tightly to exactly who needs them.\n\nThis is genuinely new insight that connects the two pages but neither states on its own. Let me preserve this as a synthesis page.",
