      "tool_uses": [
        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01XMiuNjwKAh4ry4QQQjr18E",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: How centralized resolution of runtime concerns is paired with strict scoping to prevent leakage across the Hub architecture.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - tech/dotnet\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both source pages are high-confidence architectural decisions; the pattern emerges from applying them together.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2027-01-14\\n---\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] embody a shared architectural pattern: **centralized resolution paired with strict scoping**.\\n\\n**Credential-scoping** resolves the question \\\u0022who holds sensitive data?\\\u0022 by centralizing credential injection into a single point \u2014 the startup of each child process \u2014 and scoping the API key only to that process environment, never to the Hub\u0027s own process. This prevents leakage even if the Hub is compromised.\\n\\n**Runtime-paths** resolves the question \\\u0022where are all files?\\\u0022 by centralizing path resolution into a single startup path resolver and scoping the resolved locations to consumers downstream, preventing path logic from leaking into the codebase. Adding a new runtime location means extending that one resolver, not scattering new path logic throughout the system.\\n\\nBoth decisions apply the same principle: make the sensitive or critical decision once in one place, then strictly scope access to the result. This **single composition point** pattern reduces the surface area for mistakes, makes verification straightforward, and prevents both credentials and path-discovery logic from scattering across the codebase where they would be harder to reason about and protect.\\n\u0022}"
        },
