      "assistant_text": "The index update is being denied for safety reasons. That\u0027s okay \u2014 the synthesis page itself has been successfully created. Let me answer your question based on what I found:\n\n---\n\n## Answer\n\nYour credential-scoping and runtime-path decisions reflect a shared architectural pattern: **centralized resolution paired with strict scoping**.\n\n**[[credential-scoping]]** centralizes how credentials are managed \u2014 your Anthropic API key is injected into each agent\u0027s process environment at startup, never held by the Hub itself. This scoping prevents leakage: a compromised Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment.\n\n**[[runtime-paths]]** centralizes how all file locations are determined \u2014 a single path resolver reads configuration at startup, validates inputs, and provides the resolved set to the rest of the codebase. This prevents path logic from scattering throughout the system; adding a new runtime location means extending that one resolver, not rediscovering paths in multiple places.\n\nBoth decisions apply the same principle: **make the critical decision once in one place, then strictly scope access to the result**. This pattern reduces the surface area for mistakes, makes verification straightforward, and prevents sensitive decisions (whether credentials or path discovery) from leaking into the broader codebase.\n\n---\n\nI\u0027ve saved this connection as a new page, [[concepts/single-composition-point]]. The synthesis captures how these two seemingly independent decisions actually reflect a deeper shared pattern about centralizing and scoping runtime concerns in your architecture.",
